# Home desktop (Rodimus): RTX 4080 SUPER + Ryzen iGPU.

# --- GPU userspace (kernel-independent; the kernel MODULE and matching headers
#     are resolved at bootstrap time by resolve_kernel_packages, because the
#     right package depends on which kernel is installed:
#       CachyOS kernel -> linux-cachyos-nvidia-open  (prebuilt, [cachyos])
#       Arch kernel    -> nvidia-open-dkms           (built via DKMS, extra)
#     Hardcoding nvidia-open-dkms here was a latent conflict: it Conflicts With
#     NVIDIA-MODULE, which every prebuilt linux-*-nvidia-open Provides, so the
#     list could never install cleanly on a CachyOS kernel. ---
nvidia-utils
lib32-nvidia-utils
libva-nvidia-driver

# --- Remote access: Sunshine game-stream host (connect with Moonlight) ---
# [cachyos] repo, or AUR on plain Arch without it.
sunshine

# --- Instant replay (quickshell tools menu: replay buffer + save clip) ---
gpu-screen-recorder
